#: includes/class-no-gutenberg-settings.php:157
msgid "Restore the classic Widgets screen"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-no-gutenberg-settings.php:158
msgid "Disables the block-based widget editor."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-no-gutenberg-settings.php:161
msgid "Remove block patterns and the Block Directory"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-no-gutenberg-settings.php:162
msgid "Core, theme and remote patterns are never registered."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-no-gutenberg-settings.php:165
msgid "Remove block styles and scripts from the frontend"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-no-gutenberg-settings.php:166
msgid "Takes out the block library CSS, the Global Styles inline CSS and the block scripts on every page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-no-gutenberg-settings.php:169
msgid "Neutralize theme.json and Global Styles"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-no-gutenberg-settings.php:170
msgid "Empties the theme.json data and drops the FSE theme supports, such as wide alignment or custom spacing."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-no-gutenberg-settings.php:173
msgid "Block the Site Editor"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-no-gutenberg-settings.php:174
msgid "Removes the Editor, Patterns and Fonts items under Appearance and blocks direct access to those screens."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-no-gutenberg-settings.php:177
msgid "Warn me when a block theme is active"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-no-gutenberg-settings.php:178
msgid "Shows a dismissible notice on the Dashboard and Appearance screens."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-no-gutenberg-settings.php:214
msgid "Disable Gutenberg completely"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-no-gutenberg-settings.php:217
msgid "Everything, everywhere: the block editor for every post type and user, block widgets, patterns, frontend block assets, theme.json and the Site Editor. This is how the plugin has always worked and needs no further setup. Uncheck it to choose exactly what to disable."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-no-gutenberg-settings.php:223
msgid "Also on entries that are already built with blocks"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-no-gutenberg-settings.php:226
msgid "Unchecked, an entry that contains blocks keeps the block editor whatever the rules above say, so nothing you set here can break existing content. Check it and the rules apply to everything, block content included: the Classic Editor reflows block markup, so those entries can lose their blocks the first time somebody saves them."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-no-gutenberg-settings.php:233
msgid "Disable the block editor for..."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-no-gutenberg-settings.php:235
msgid "Rules are independent: anything that matches gets the Classic Editor. Leave every rule empty and the block editor stays available."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-no-gutenberg-settings.php:240
msgid "WooCommerce products play by these same rules: check Products below to force the classic product editor. Its block styles are removed with the rest of the frontend block assets."
msgstr ""

